Apart from other things that I do I also write a few bash scripts!
hurrah!

Conlock is a little console locking utility that basically traps the
kill, ctrl+c and ctrl+d signals.. it also presents you with a password
to type that's then hashed with md5sum and checked against a file in
the current users home directory.

Conlock is available from my site:
http://downstairscomputer.no-ip.org:81/me/projects/conlock-0.02.tar.gz

My site is up between 11AM and 9PM GMT for the next 3 weeks and then
i'm going on holidays.. so it won't be up during either july or
august..

Feedback is welcome..

version 0.02 ChangeLog is:
Both the config script and conlock are now aware of the root user, so
if you're root. conlock'll write the config file to /root..

Infi also provided me with the wisdom that is the ability to
background jobs in bash.. I squished that bug good!

